WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.904
Habits are repeated behavior patterns supported by cues, actions, and consequences.

00:00:03.904 --> 00:00:07.016
A cue makes the behavior more likely to start.

00:00:07.016 --> 00:00:09.091
The action is the behavior itself.

00:00:09.091 --> 00:00:13.932
The consequence, whether obvious or subtle, influences whether the pattern is likely to repeat.

00:00:13.932 --> 00:00:18.081
Over time, repeated cue-behavior-consequence patterns can become easier to trigger and perform.

00:00:18.081 --> 00:00:21.539
This is one reason relying only on willpower is fragile.

00:00:21.539 --> 00:00:23.960
A person may intend to behave differently,

00:00:23.960 --> 00:00:26.726
but the environment keeps triggering the old pattern.

00:00:26.726 --> 00:00:30.530
If the phone is visible, the distraction is one tap away.

00:00:30.530 --> 00:00:34.334
If the checklist is buried, the desired behavior takes extra effort.

00:00:34.334 --> 00:00:37.100
If the team rewards speed but not quality,

00:00:37.100 --> 00:00:40.212
rushed work may become the path of least resistance.

00:00:40.212 --> 00:00:42.979
Environment design changes the pattern by changing friction.

00:00:42.979 --> 00:00:47.474
Reduce friction for desired behaviors and increase friction for distractions or unwanted patterns.

00:00:47.474 --> 00:00:50.932
Put the practice material where it is easy to start.

00:00:50.932 --> 00:00:52.661
Make the next step visible.

00:00:52.661 --> 00:00:55.427
Remove avoidable cues for behaviors that interrupt focus.

00:00:55.427 --> 00:00:58.540
Use routines that make the desired action more automatic,

00:00:58.540 --> 00:01:00.960
especially at the start of a session.

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:04.418
Replacing patterns is usually more practical than only suppressing them.

00:01:04.418 --> 00:01:08.568
Instead of saying, stop procrastinating, define the cue and the replacement action.

00:01:08.568 --> 00:01:12.717
When I open the project folder, I write the next visible step.

00:01:12.717 --> 00:01:16.867
When I finish a meeting, I capture one decision and one follow-up.

00:01:16.867 --> 00:01:21.016
Neuroplasticity supports habit change over time, but the change needs repetition, feedback,

00:01:21.016 --> 00:01:24.820
and a system that makes the new behavior easier to repeat.
